Subject: [P5] Gate reconstruction on compiled K/codebook support
Base-commit: 15ded2f3add148c4db3c900cba7de878238f53bc
Status: local-only draft; PROVISIONAL — NOT FOR PUBLIC HEADLINE
D5 anchors: exl3xpu/ops.py:100-103 and public routing :130-137.
D5 derivation: exported exl3_reconstruct exists in K4/K6-only builds but
K3 dispatch is compiled out; hasattr passes and engine-init large-M throws.
Require compiled support plus actual reconstruction pair set; unsupported
K3 falls back to Triton, enabled K3 reaches C++ small AND large M.
Also keep K6/cb0/1 out of the large-M C++ route (GEMM advertises them but
reconstruct does not). Integer metadata check only, no tensor scalar reads.
Capture-safety: no new allocation or device sync. Existing fallback/private
scratch behavior is not certified; whole-op D3 HOLD. Test added is CPU-only.

